---
import Reference from '../../layouts/reference.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const code = `import { ParticleEffect } from '@reparticle/pixi';

// Use your existing, initialized Pixi application.
const effect = new ParticleEffect({
  version: 1,
  emitters: [{
    id: 'sparks',
    capacity: 2048,
    seed: 42,
    emission: { rate: 120, shape: { type: 'point' } },
    initial: {
      lifetime: 2,
      speed: 90,
      direction: -Math.PI / 2,
      spread: Math.PI / 2,
      size: 12,
    },
  }],
}, { ticker: app.ticker });
effect.position.set(app.screen.width / 2, app.screen.height / 2);
app.stage.addChild(effect);`;
const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'install', text: 'Install' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'add-particles-to-a-pixijs-scene', text: 'Add particles to a PixiJS scene' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'use-your-own-texture', text: 'Use your own texture' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'control-playback', text: 'Control playback' },
];
---
<Reference headings={headings} title="Quick start" description="Add reparticle to your PixiJS app. Create an effect and add it to the stage.">
  <h2 id={headings[0].slug}>{headings[0].text}</h2><Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={'npm install @reparticle/pixi'} lang="sh" />
  <p>This guide assumes you already have a PixiJS application using v8.20.1 or later within v8. The core engine is included as a dependency of <code>@reparticle/pixi</code>.</p>
  <p>Your PixiJS app must use WebGL2.</p>
  <h2 id={headings[1].slug}>{headings[1].text}</h2><Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={code} lang="ts" />
  <p>The effect starts automatically using your app’s ticker. Without artwork, it renders with the built-in fallback texture.</p>
  <h2 id={headings[2].slug}>{headings[2].text}</h2><Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={`import { Assets } from 'pixi.js';

const sparkTexture = await Assets.load('/textures/spark.png');
effect.setEmitterTexture('sparks', { textures: [sparkTexture] });`} lang="ts" />
  <p>This updates the effect created above. The <code>sparks</code> argument matches the emitter ID in the definition. See <a href={`${base}docs/textures/`}>Textures &amp; animation</a> for atlas frames and flipbooks.</p>
  <h2 id={headings[3].slug}>{headings[3].text}</h2><Code theme="github-dark-dimmed" code={`effect.pause();            // Pause.
effect.resume();           // Continue.
effect.reset();            // Restart from the beginning.
effect.stop();             // Stop emitting; let existing particles finish.
effect.retire();           // Finish the current loop, then stop emitting.
effect.destroy();          // Remove and release the effect.`} lang="ts" />
  <p>Destroy the effect when removing the scene. Textures supplied by your application remain yours to manage.</p>
</Reference>
